{
  "A window or a dialog on a native `<dialog>`: one form, shown modeless or modal by whoever shows it. It has a title bar, moves, resizes, minimizes and maximizes; Enter and Escape press its buttons; forms open forms. `messageBox` and `confirm` cover the common questions.": "",
  "In JSX, `x-model` shows the form while the value is true and writes `false` when the user closes it; it is hidden, not disposed, and lives with its parent. Programmatically, a form (often a class with a `view()`) is shown with `show(host)` or `showDialog(host)`; it is added to the host and disposed when it closes.": "",
  "Modal and modeless": "",
  "`show()` keeps the page usable: several modeless windows stack, a click brings one to the front. `showDialog()` blocks everything else until it closes; a modal form opened from a modal one blocks that one too.": "",
  "Title bar and frame": "",
  "The title bar shows the icon, the title and the buttons you switch on. The form moves by its title bar and stays inside the viewport; it resizes from its edges and corners down to the `window.min-*` tokens. Every part has its own switch.": "",
  "Default and cancel buttons": "",
  "Enter in a one-line field clicks `acceptButton`; Escape clicks `cancelButton`. Without a cancel button, `closeOnEscape` decides: on for modal forms, off for modeless ones.": "",
  "`onClosing` can keep the form open, here while it has changes; `reason` tells the user (close button, Escape) programmatically and from the owner going away.": "",
  "Message boxes": "",
  "`messageBox` shows a modal message with buttons and resolves with the result of the one pressed; `confirm` asks OK or Cancel and resolves `true` or `false`. Caution and danger boxes are alert dialogs; a danger box starts on its safe button.": "",
  "Inside a modal form Tab goes round; from a modeless one it goes on to the page.": "",
  "Clicks `cancelButton`; else closes it when `closeOnEscape` (on for modal forms).": "",
  "In a one-line field: clicks `acceptButton` (not in a text area, not on a button).": "",
  "Access keys work inside the front window; while a modal form is open, only inside it.": "",
  "With the pointer. There are no keys of its own; an app can add them with `form.addShortcut(...)` and the `left` / `top` / `width` / `height` properties.": "",
  "A native `<dialog>`: `showModal()` for a modal form (the browser makes the page inert), `show()` for a modeless one.": "",
  "`role=\"dialog\"` (`alertdialog` with `alert`), `aria-modal=\"true\"` when modal, named by its title through `aria-labelledby`.": "",
  "A message box is described by its text (`aria-describedby`).": "",
  "On open: `[autofocus]`, the first field, the accept button, the first control. On close: back where it was. Never on `<body>`.": "",
  "Named from `uiLocale` (Minimize, Maximize, Restore, Close).": "",
  "A short fade with the motion tokens; none under reduced motion.": "",
  "The title bar buttons and the `ok`, `cancel`, `yes`, `no` buttons of a message box are named from `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "The `<dialog>`. `data-state` (`normal`, `minimized`, `maximized`), `data-modal`, `data-active`, `data-placed`, `data-docked`, `data-resizable`, `data-movable`, `data-dragging`.": "",
  "The title bar and its parts.": "",
  "The content area and the buttons row.": "",
  "The resize handles.": "",
  "The chip a minimized form leaves in its `minimizeTarget`.": "",
  "A message box’s content; `data-tone`.": "",
  "The size and place the form writes on itself.": "",
  "Units: behind a modal form; the surface (`active`, `dialog`: a modal one, `maximized`).": "",
  "Units: the title bar (`active`, `dialog`), its icon, the title (`dialog`) and its buttons.": "",
  "Units: the content area, the buttons row, the resize grips (`corner`).": "",
  "The title bar’s height (from the design system’s `bar.*`), where the title sits, where its buttons sit.": "",
  "The smallest size and the room kept around it.": "",
  "The resize handles; how far it slides in.": "",
  "Message boxes: units for the content and its tone glyph (per tone), and their width.": "",
  "Opened through `value`, it is modal.": "",
  "The title in the title bar; it names the form. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "What fills the content area, next to JSX children and `view()`.": "",
  "A row under the content that does not scroll, for the buttons.": "",
  "An icon at the start of the title bar.": "",
  "The close button.": "",
  "The minimize button; modeless forms only.": "",
  "The maximize button; a double click on the title bar does the same.": "",
  "Resized from its edges and corners.": "",
  "Moved by dragging the title bar; it stays inside the viewport.": "",
  "modal: `true`, modeless: `false`": "",
  "Escape closes it with `cancel` when there is no `cancelButton`.": "",
  "The button Enter clicks from a one-line field.": "",
  "The button Escape clicks.": "",
  "Where a minimized form leaves a chip that brings it back. Without it the form folds to its title bar.": "",
  "`center`, or `manual` at `left` and `top`.": "",
  "With `manual`: the place, from the start edge (the right one in RTL) and the top. A number is pixels.": "",
  "content size": "",
  "A CSS length; a number is pixels.": "",
  "`role=\"alertdialog\"`: something urgent.": "",
  "Default: disposed when `show` / `showDialog` added it to the host; a JSX form is hidden.": "",
  "A value or a function, like the prop. `left`, `top`, `width` and `height` follow the user moving and resizing it.": "",
  "How it closed, or will: `close()` without an argument uses it. `cancel` when it opens.": "",
  "Open; shown modal; the front window of the page.": "",
  "The control inside that has focus or had it last.": "",
  "The content area element.": "",
  "Shows it modeless in `host` (a component or the application); it dies with `disposeRef`, else the host.": "",
  "Shows it modal; resolves with the result when it closes.": "",
  "Brings it to the front with focus on its last active control.": "",
  "Set `windowState`.": "",
  "Puts it back in the middle of the viewport.": "",
  "Focus back to its last active control.": "",
  "Before it is shown the first time: the place to fill it.": "",
  "It became the front window / another one did.": "",
  "It is about to close. `e`: `{ result, reason, source, cancel }`; `cancel = true` keeps it open (not when its owner is going away).": "",
  "It closed. `e`: `{ result, reason, source }`; `reason` is `user` (close button, Escape), `code` or `owner`.": "",
  "Helpers": "",
  "A modal message: `title`, `text`, `buttons` (`ok`, `cancel`, `yes`, `no` or `{ text, result, tone }`), `tone` (`info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`), `defaultButton`, `host`.": "",
  "OK and Cancel; `true` for OK.": ""
}
